From: ericek111 <erik.brocko@letemsvetemapplem.eu>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:42:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/47] NMXVGAFB: scan presented surfaces out of their own
 pages (nmxScanoutSurface)

NMXAccel can hand over the surface it is presenting; the framebuffer makes the surface's pages a
virtio-gpu blob (scatter list, up to 4000 runs; the command area grows to 64 KB), switches scanout 0
to it and flushes. Blobs are cached per surface (8, LRU, never the one on screen), the memory
prepared while cached. nmxScanoutHome returns to the framebuffer's own buffer before a copy.
The VBL flush now runs under the scan-out lock: flushing the blob that was just replaced is refused
by QEMU (INVALID_PARAMETER), which had switched the virtio scan-out off; only a command timeout does.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DP5dwQG4pUvK6V9ftNsQRB
